        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "Teacher: You're also not limited to interacting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 7.59,
          "en": "with the request in an intersetter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 10.56,
          "en": "You can also interact with the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.56,
          "end": 13.68,
          "en": "You do this by adding something here to handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.68,
          "end": 16.47,
          "en": "because handle actually gives you an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.47,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "which I guess makes sense because in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 22.23,
          "en": "your request isn't observable to which you subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.23,
          "end": 23.063,
          "en": "in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.063,
          "end": 26.82,
          "en": "So this in the end is the request with the response in it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.82,
          "end": 29.43,
          "en": "you could say, wrapped into an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.43,
          "end": 32.28,
          "en": "and therefore here you can, of course, add pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.28,
          "end": 35.46,
          "en": "and do something with the response if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.46,
          "end": 38.31,
          "en": "You could add the MAP operator here to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.31,
          "end": 39.87,
          "en": "the response, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "Of course, you should be careful with that and not change it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 44.84,
          "en": "in a way that the rest of your application breaks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 50.49,
          "en": "or what I'll do here, you use tap, which you need to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 55.49,
          "en": "from RXJS Operators, to simply look into the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 58.41,
          "en": "Now here in tap you get an event that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.41,
          "end": 60.18,
          "en": "You always get events here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.18,
          "end": 62.94,
          "en": "Remember I showed you that you can observe different kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "of responses with the angle or HTTP client no matter what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 68.78999999999999,
          "en": "you chose there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.78999999999999,
          "end": 72.87,
          "en": "Here in the intersetter, you always get an event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.87,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "so that you have the most granular access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 78.33,
          "en": "to the response you could possibly have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.33,
          "end": 81.99,
          "en": "So here for example, we could check if the event type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.99,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "is equal to the HTTP event type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 89.24,
          "en": "which you also need to import of response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.76,
          "end": 93.57,
          "en": "because here maybe I only care about that response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.57,
          "end": 97.35,
          "en": "I will log the event before that, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.35,
          "end": 101.22999999999999,
          "en": "so that we can see all events we got and then in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.87,
          "end": 107.87,
          "en": "we could say response arrived, body data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.37,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "and then simply console log the event body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 116.283,
          "en": "which here is the response body, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 119.13,
          "en": "Now, here again, I'm just doing some logging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.13,
          "end": 121.92,
          "en": "but as I just mentioned, you could use other operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.92,
          "end": 124.53,
          "en": "like map here and even transform the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.53,
          "end": 125.853,
          "en": "That would be possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.84,
          "end": 129.39,
          "en": "So now if we save that and we go back and we have a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 131.91,
          "en": "at the console, we see a bunch of output there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.91,
          "end": 134.4,
          "en": "Let me clear it to make it a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.4,
          "end": 137.34,
          "en": "and fetch posts again and now you see request is on its way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.34,
          "end": 139.29,
          "en": "Then we have type zero, which is this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.29,
          "end": 141.6,
          "en": "The request is now sent event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.6,
          "end": 144.51,
          "en": "Then we got the response, therefore we now got that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 148.02,
          "en": "response arrived log and there indeed, we now see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.02,
          "end": 150.39,
          "en": "the response body being locked because that is what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.39,
          "end": 151.77,
          "en": "I'm doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.77,
          "end": 153.03,
          "en": "So this is possible too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 155.94,
          "en": "You cannot just interact with the request inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.94,
          "end": 157.14,
          "en": "of your intersetter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.14,
          "end": 160.17000000000002,
          "en": "You can also interact with the response if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.17000000000002,
          "end": 162.54,
          "en": "You can log it, you can manipulate it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
